2026-07-15 15:45:02,995 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To meet the regulatory requirements outlined in the tender, our company, Faber IA, already has several security measures in place. For GDPR compliance, we have achieved ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the scope of development, delivery, and operations. Additionally, our ISO 27701 certification provides a privacy information management extension. 

We utilize encryption in transit with TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest with AES-256, ensuring that data is protected both during transmission and when stored. Our key management system is based on EU-based infrastructure, further enhancing security.

Regarding pseudonymisation, we have this capability in place for sensitive data where relevant. We also practice data minimization and have configurable retention policies aligned with legal archival obligations. 

To ensure the segregation of duties and prevent any conflicts of interest, we maintain a strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) system and audit logging of access and every system output. The appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) and the maintenance of a data processing register are also part of our compliance framework.

For professional secrecy and confidentiality, we are familiar with the requirements of professional secrecy, particularly for clients bound by such obligations, including national professional orders.

To comply with anti-money-laundering obligations (LCB-FT), we are aware of the need not to undermine a firm's reporting obligations. Our experience with statutory audit principles includes auditor independence and separation of duties, ensuring that our solutions respect these critical aspects.

Demonstrating compliance can be achieved through our existing certifications (ISO 27001 and ISO 27701), regular audits by external providers (equivalent to CREST level for penetration testing), and adherence to our vulnerability management process with remediation SLAs. Our incident response plan, including a 72-hour GDPR breach notification workflow, further ensures readiness in case of security incidents.

We also host data within the EU through our partnership with OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer. This supports sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU and aligns with the requirement for no data transfer outside the EU.

By leveraging these existing measures and certifications, Faber IA can demonstrate a strong foundation for meeting the regulatory requirements outlined in the tender, including GDPR compliance, professional secrecy, auditor independence, and anti-money-laundering obligations.
